        <briefdescription>
<para>Ascon-XOF128 extendable-output digest. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Computes <computeroutput>digest_size</computeroutput> bytes of output from <computeroutput>message</computeroutput> using the Ascon-XOF128 sponge construction defined in Algorithm 9 of NIST SP 800-232 Section 5.2.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">message</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input message buffer. May be <computeroutput>NULL</computeroutput> if and only if <computeroutput>message_size</computeroutput> is zero, in which case the XOF output over the empty string is produced. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">message_size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Byte length of <computeroutput>message</computeroutput>. May be zero. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">digest</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Destination buffer for the output digest. The caller is responsible for providing a buffer of at least <computeroutput>digest_size</computeroutput> bytes. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">digest_size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Desired output length in bytes. Must be greater than zero.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>digest</computeroutput> is non-NULL. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>message</computeroutput> is non-NULL when <computeroutput>message_size</computeroutput> is greater than zero. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>message</computeroutput> points to a readable buffer of at least <computeroutput>message_size</computeroutput> bytes. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>digest</computeroutput> points to a writable buffer of at least <computeroutput>digest_size</computeroutput> bytes. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>digest_size</computeroutput> is greater than zero. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>message</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>digest</computeroutput> do not overlap. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
